  "narrative": "All estimates below are already signed to the stated hypothesis direction. For dependency_composite, a claim is accepted only when the signed point estimate exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units and the uncertainty is strong enough to support a threshold-exceeding effect in the claimed direction. The most important new result is H37, MSI-high: R73 gives signed +0.775 with interval +0.664 to +0.885, n 130 exposed and 1870 comparator. Because direction is -1, this corresponds to a raw lower composite dependency score in MSI-high samples, i.e. stronger measured dependency. The effect is far above threshold and interval-supported in discovery, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association. I request independent validation because this is a new large signal emerging after many multiplicity-heavy comparisons and because MSI-high could be correlated with mutation burden, genomic co-alterations, or screen features not controlled in the unadjusted Welch comparison. Validation does not establish causality or external generalizability, but it tests reproducibility within the supplied dataset. H94 was the pre-specified final PTEN context: PTEN loss in TP53-intact, adenocarcinoma, Avana-library, high-screen-quality samples. R66 gives signed +0.157 with interval +0.015 to +0.299 and only 78 exposed cells. The point estimate barely exceeds threshold, but the interval includes substantial values below threshold and near zero. Given prior PTEN validation failure and the multiplicity of PTEN contexts, this is not accepted; I leave it unresolved and close this final PTEN confirmation branch to avoid further stratum mining. PTEN remains a suggestive but not mature dataset-specific predictor. The interaction results for established predictors are not support for context dependence: H95 SMARCA4-by-EMT R67 is small and opposite claimed amplification; H96 TP53-by-EMT R68 is essentially null; H97 KEAP1-by-EMT R69 is small and opposite; H98 KEAP1-by-hypoxia R70 is small and below threshold; H101 KRAS-by-high mutation burden R71 is below threshold with interval crossing zero. All are rejected and closed. H102 STK11 in adenocarcinoma R72 is +0.046 with interval crossing zero, so it does not rescue the broad STK11 null and is rejected and closed. The broad genomic scans H48 APC, H49 SMAD4, H50 NF1, and H52 BRCA2 are all small or interval-compatible with no meaningful threshold effect and are rejected and closed. Overall, the mature supported dataset-specific associations remain SMARCA4 loss toward stronger dependency, TP53 loss toward weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss toward weaker dependency, plus the newly discovery-supported MSI-high association toward stronger dependency, pending validation. These are associations in this dataset, not causal or mechanistic claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current mature dataset-specific accepted associations: H3 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger dependency; H13 TP53 loss -> weaker dependency; H38 KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency; H37 MSI-high -> stronger dependency accepted in discovery and under independent validation request because of multiplicity and possible confounding. PTEN is downgraded: H94 final pre-specified PTEN context is point-barely-above-threshold but imprecise and interval-crossing, so unresolved/closed; do not further mine PTEN unless a new independent scheduled validation changes the evidence. Broad PTEN and TP53-wildtype PTEN remain borderline only; H40 independent validation did not clear threshold. CDKN2A remains borderline/unresolved but not accepted. Context interactions tested for SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1 by EMT, hypoxia, aneuploidy, screen quality, mutation burden, culture, and TP53 loss are mostly null or small and closed. Broad negative/absent threshold evidence: STK11 broad and in adenocarcinoma, KRAS, MYC amp, ARID1A, MTAP, RB1, EGFR amp, ERBB2 amp, BRAF V600E, PIK3CA, APC, SMAD4, NF1, BRCA2, research markers, sex positive claim, media serum 10 vs 5, Avana main effect, matched omics/CRISPR QC main effect. Next priorities: await H37 validation; then test MSI-high robustness by mutation-burden strata, TP53-intact status, and high screen quality to assess confounding and technical dependence. Keep H99/H100 culture interactions, H103 media 5 vs 2, H104 Ky library, H105 RNA-omics availability deferred unless they become more plausible. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations; causality and generalizability unresolved.",
